Kilómetro Cero — 3D circuit mode
================================

This directory is a derivative work, separate from the Phaser game at the root
of this repository. This NOTICE records what was inherited, what was added, and
what was removed. See ../NOTICE for the root project.


1. UPSTREAM WORK
----------------

The 3D mode is derived from:

    react-racing-game
    https://github.com/colyseus/react-racing-game
    Licensed under the MIT License

which is itself a fork of:

    @pmndrs/racing-game
    Copyright 2021 pmndrs, contributors
    https://github.com/pmndrs/racing-game
    Licensed under the MIT License

The upstream repository was cloned into this directory and its .git removed.
Everything here that is not listed in section 4 descends from that project — in
particular the React Three Fiber application shell: the @react-three/cannon
raycast-vehicle physics, the chase/first-person/bird's-eye cameras, the dust,
skid, boost and engine-audio effects, the zustand store and key bindings, and
the whole HUD (clock, speedometer, help, colour picker, minimap, leaderboard).

The vehicle *tuning* and the chase camera's behaviour are no longer upstream's.
Engine force, grip, suspension, steering lock and its speed sensitivity, the
boost, the field of view and its animation with speed, and the camera's easing
and distance were all re-tuned against a headless measuring rig; the structure
is still theirs. README.md, "Making it arcade", records the before and after.

The upstream MIT licence text is reproduced verbatim in LICENSE.md and continues
to govern this work. The typo in its copyright line ("pmdrs") is upstream's; it
is left untouched.


