4. ADDED BY THIS PROJECT
------------------------

Original work by the Kilómetro Cero contributors, MIT licensed:

  - scripts/fit-circuit.mjs — aligns the circuit model to the projected geodata
    (ICP on the model's TarmacDark mesh, trimmed least squares, rigid) and then
    measures the road off the aligned model: the middle of the paved corridor,
    both asphalt edges, the surface height and the cross-slope, 1024 times
    around the lap. Writes src/circuit/fit.json and src/circuit/road.ts.
  - scripts/build-circuit-model.mjs — the compression pipeline described in
    section 2.
  - src/circuit/ — layout.ts turns the generated road samples into arc length,
    signed curvature and an orthonormal road frame per sample, and finds La
    Monumental by curvature analysis; walls.ts places the invisible collision
    boxes on the measured asphalt edges. What is derived from real data and what
    is our approximation is set out in README.md.
  - src/models/track/Circuit.tsx, CircuitPhysics.tsx, Ground.tsx and
    LapTiming.tsx — the model renderer, the trimesh + wall collision, the catch
    plane, and sector/lap timing.
  - src/models/track/Crowd.tsx — the crowd. Finds the seating surfaces in the
    model's four grandstand materials (upward-facing triangles, filtered by
    area and by headroom) and scatters ~6,000 instanced spectators over them,
    two draw calls in total. The circuit model has none; see section 2.
  - src/models/Killzone.tsx — replaces upstream's six-plane BoundingBox, which
    was in permanent contact with everything inside it.
  - src/frame.ts — a frame-time clamp; several upstream smoothing terms diverge
    below about 20 fps.
  - src/draco.ts — points the loader at the vendored decoder.

No file in this directory is covered by a copyright carve-out. Everything here
is redistributable under the MIT License in LICENSE.md.


